WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Driving the Need for Product and Process Measurement

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Hello, Mike Harry, and welcome to this segment on measurement power.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.600
We’re going to be looking at the absolute power of how measurements

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.866
can create improvement. Measurements are needed

5
00:00:18.866 --> 00:00:22.866
to guide our way through process improvement.

6
00:00:22.866 --> 00:00:25.866
And to sustain that process improvement.

7
00:00:25.866 --> 00:00:31.332
Without a doubt measurement is power. Just as knowledge is power.

8
00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:35.133
Without measurements, it becomes very difficult

9
00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:42.099
to fly our plane, so to speak, literally and figuratively.

10
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.566
You see, these measurements are absolutely essential.

11
00:00:46.566 --> 00:00:49.566
How would we fly an airplane without them?

12
00:00:49.566 --> 00:00:56.599
Can you imagine getting on board an airliner and the pilot has no instruments?

13
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:01.466
Because measurement is at the base of instrumentation.

14
00:01:01.466 --> 00:01:06.332
And instrumentation tells us what's going on.

15
00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:11.799
That simple. We gotta be able to know that.

16
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.166
Understand where we’re at. Where we’re going.

17
00:01:16.166 --> 00:01:19.032
And how to improve. Measurements are essential for that.
